1
00:00:13,221 --> 00:00:15,432
Hey, Roman! Hey!

2
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:18,935
Huh? He's gone. Guess he couldn't hear me.

3
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:21,229
No use calling him
when he's got his camera out.

4
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:22,313
No use?

5
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:24,190
He can’t hear you.
Gets all wrapped up.

6
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:25,567
In what?

7
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:26,651
His camera.

8
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:27,944
Why would he care about that?

9
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,696
Says he likes it.

10
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,948
Does he use it for BD and stuff?

11
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:34,451
No, he likes cinema.

12
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,704
"Cinema"? What's a "cinema"?

13
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:40,957
Such a gonkbrain...

14
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:44,461
You watch 'em on a screen in a dark room.

15
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:48,214
Know-it-all! You even been to one?

16
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:50,091
I mean... No...

17
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:52,046
You... don't work here, do you?

18
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:06,895
That's 30 seconds
we don't get back, Miguel.

19
00:03:06,978 --> 00:03:08,396
Get it together.

20
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:10,648
S-sorry 'bout that, King.

21
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:13,484
Just leave the body!

22
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:16,779
Miguel. You're too sloppy.

23
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:20,491
Hey, can we not tell Emily about this?

24
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:26,873
Fuck! These boxes all look the same!

25
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:29,125
Chill, Miguel. Knew this might happen.

26
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,335
So which is ours?

27
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:34,339
Left side... that row.
Hop two to the right... Bingo.

28
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:40,094
Find it?

29
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:41,554
Are we sure?

30
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:42,889
Hold it up for me?

31
00:03:42,972 --> 00:03:45,850
AR-CPRN-XR-05.

32
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:47,852
Yep, that's our mark.

33
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,229
Got it!

34
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:50,980
What the hell are you doing?

35
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:54,817
Hey! Careful with it.
Case has a biochip inside!

36
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:55,902
Avida?

37
00:03:55,985 --> 00:03:58,112
Yeah, yeah. I know!

38
00:03:58,196 --> 00:03:59,906
Phew, it's cold!

39
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:01,824
Target secured.

40
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:04,369
...Hey! Said we got the case!

41
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,789
King! You hear me?

42
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:15,255
What, Miguel? You got the case?

43
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:17,090
Hey... C'mon, man...

44
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:19,092
We have it! Let's delta!

45
00:04:19,175 --> 00:04:21,552
Seriously, guys...

46
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:23,346
Our ride?

47
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:25,223
Hacked the one sitting out front.

48
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:26,557
And our wheelman?

49
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:29,602
Not included! Better figure it out...

50
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:31,479
...Hold on.

51
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:33,982
Somethin' wrong?

52
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:36,985
- Hey, Meshuga?
- Shit! Fall ba--

53
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:39,612
The door!

54
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:43,825
King! Run a scan!

55
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:06,889
Miguel!

56
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:26,659
Hey! Hold it right--

57
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:31,956
Miguel, the car!

58
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,624
I know!

59
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,086
Yo, that a fire?

60
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,130
Ain't that Arasaka turf?

61
00:05:39,922 --> 00:05:43,176
What's this? Could it
be major breaking news?

62
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:45,470
Eh, I wish...

63
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:51,601
Not takin' my eyes off--

64
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,228
Hey! Watch where you're... walking...

65
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:56,606
- Freeze! Stop right there, or--
- The fuck did you say, kid?

66
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:58,858
Whoa! S-s-s-sorry!

67
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:12,705
Shit! What is it with today?

68
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:16,459
Emily, are you okay? Hey!

69
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:18,044
More or less...

70
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:20,755
King! The fuck is your problem, old man?

71
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:23,007
Miguel, the case...

72
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:25,343
Just leave it! The gig's a bust.

73
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:27,470
Hey! Stop where you are!

74
00:06:34,977 --> 00:06:36,104
Avida...

75
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:47,406
Avida!

76
00:06:57,083 --> 00:06:58,835
Avida!

77
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:21,149
C'mon, Emily. Hang in there.

78
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:24,652
We... we gotta get you to a clinic...

79
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:30,116
Forget it... Save yourself and run, Miguel.

80
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:34,495
Don't say shit like that!
Fuck... What's wrong with King?

81
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:36,414
Cyberpsychosis.

82
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:38,916
I saw it when our eyes met.

83
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:42,712
That look in his eyes... He's gone psycho.

84
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:56,934
———... ——— at ——— Cyberpsycho...

85
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:08,988
What a mess.

86
00:08:09,572 --> 00:08:12,658
Hey. Clockin' in.

87
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:14,952
Uh, whatcha watchin'?

88
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:16,412
A freelance video.

89
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:19,790
Video? But we're a BD shop.

90
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:22,960
There's still a market
for vids like these too.

91
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:26,088
Oh! This that Arasaka thing
from yesterday's newsfeed?

92
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:29,008
Yup. MaxTac tried to bag a 'psycho...

93
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:33,513
Only the bastard
had VIP platinum coverage.

94
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:36,224
Trauma Team came rushing in to save him.

95
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:39,310
Arasaka was the only one left eatin' shit.

96
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:43,648
Is Arasaka slippin' or what? Feels like
they're takin' big hits more than ever.

97
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:47,235
- Hey, did you film this?
- Yeah.

98
00:08:47,318 --> 00:08:48,945
Huh. Not bad.

99
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,242
Oh, and there's Trauma Team.

100
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:59,163
Old man was doin' good for his age,
but he's finally down for the count.

101
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:00,456
He famous?

102
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:01,749
Goes by "King."

103
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:04,669
"King"? So lame!

104
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:07,296
Right? Think that's bad,
wait'll I tell ya his real name--

105
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:08,506
So, what's it worth?

106
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:14,679
- Two hundo.
- That's cheap. Stupidly cheap.

107
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:17,014
Forget it! The news would pay way more!

108
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:21,018
N54 might cough up a hundred, tops.

109
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,522
Fine... 200.

110
00:09:26,315 --> 00:09:28,067
Kinda childish of you.

111
00:09:29,485 --> 00:09:33,364
Quit yappin' and get back to work!
Those raw BDs won't tune themselves!

112
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:35,533
Yeah, yeah...

113
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:38,661
Bye-bye, then.

114
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,871
Ugh, back to the grind...

115
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:53,718
Look, Roman. You wanna make money,
it's all BDs now. Braindance.

116
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:58,139
Got any idea the kind of eddies
Jessie rakes in with tunejobs these days?

117
00:09:58,222 --> 00:10:01,601
Calling BD tuning "editing" is a stretch.

118
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:05,187
It's not the same as cutting video.
BDs are just relived memories.

119
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:06,647
Where's the fun in that?

120
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:09,317
Man oh man, were you
born in the wrong century.

121
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:13,571
The people want BDs.
Not the videos you like.

122
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:16,657
Film's dead.

123
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,494
You can't tell stories with BDs.

124
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:23,331
Stories? Who needs 'em?

125
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:28,336
BDs have no boundaries. Nothing
separates the audience from the action.

126
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:33,341
Films have screens. But great films
pull you right through that boundary.

127
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:35,176
You forget the screen's there.

128
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:37,219
That's why they matter.

129
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:40,222
That's why stories matter.

130
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:43,225
Little fuckin' philosophizer...

131
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:47,563
If you don't wanna scroll BDs,
then try scrollin' Maelstrom.

132
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:50,858
Maelstrom? Those guys're dangerous.

133
00:10:50,941 --> 00:10:52,860
Thought you needed the money.

134
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:57,657
Footage of them chippin' chrome ain't easy
to come by, but that shit's a hot seller.

135
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:02,119
That's practically snuff! There's no art
in that! Plus, where would I even start?

136
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:04,163
Figure it out!

137
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:06,666
If it was easy, it wouldn't
be worth a damn!

138
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:10,211
Land me a reel, and I'll pay ya enough
to get a top-shelf camera.

139
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:13,464
But good cams aren't even
on the market in the first place.

140
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:19,220
35mm. I've got a 35mm.

141
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:25,351
Got film, too. Not sure
the fossil still works though...

142
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:30,606
Get that footage, she's yours.
Or else, there's always BDs.

143
00:11:31,273 --> 00:11:33,234
Maelstrom, huh?

144
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:38,030
Talia, stop! You're not
getting away this time!

145
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:40,241
Hey... Talia! I said stop! Tali--

146
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:43,160
- Talia!
- Miss Yang again?

147
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:44,620
How many times is that?

148
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:47,248
The patient is awake.

149
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:51,502
Fifty days? I was asleep for that long?

150
00:11:51,585 --> 00:11:53,504
Pretty wild, right?

151
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,464
But at least you're alive.

152
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:58,968
If you didn't have platinum coverage,
you'd be in a MaxTac body bag right now.

153
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:00,761
Sure is worth the fat price tag.

154
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,054
In a body bag?

155
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:03,347
MaxTac?

156
00:12:03,431 --> 00:12:07,476
That's right. You nearly had
a full cyberpsychotic break.

157
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,229
Cyberpsychosis? Me?

158
00:12:10,312 --> 00:12:12,648
Hate to say it,
but you overdid the chrome.

159
00:12:12,731 --> 00:12:15,526
There's a limit to how much
the human body can handle.

160
00:12:15,609 --> 00:12:18,779
Add stress and whatever
else on top of that, and well...

161
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:21,782
No, I was at my peak.

162
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:23,951
Never felt any stress...

163
00:12:24,034 --> 00:12:27,163
It's fairly common
to show no signs or symptoms.

164
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:31,250
Truth is, there's still a lot we don't
understand about what triggers it.

165
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:33,711
But your case was darn near textbook.

166
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:36,338
You pushed past your limit.
That's just the fact of it.

167
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:41,469
We've cut the nonessential hardware
and swapped in low-draw alternatives.

168
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:46,307
Don't worry about your brain goin'
boom for now. Give ya my word.

169
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:48,434
So how long?

170
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:51,145
How long before I can use them--

171
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:53,689
Don't be stupid, choom. You tryna die?

172
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:56,317
Absolutely no chrome, ever.

173
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,610
You're kidding?

174
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:59,820
The moment you plug back in...

175
00:12:59,904 --> 00:13:00,946
Kaboom!

176
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:03,699
And you don't have insurance
to protect you anymore.

177
00:13:03,782 --> 00:13:06,577
There's no stoppin' MaxTac
next time they come for you.

178
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:09,330
Well, that's that.

179
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:12,500
Now, let's talk about your bill.

180
00:13:12,583 --> 00:13:16,587
Good thing you saved up!
Care like this would bankrupt most people!

181
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:20,341
We had to repo a few things to
cover the shortfall, but you're all set!

182
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:21,592
God bless you!

183
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:36,482
- King! You're alive?
- Apparently.

184
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:38,901
I mean... that's great.

185
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:41,153
Hey, did you say "King"?

186
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,989
That Miguel? You boys at the Afterlife?

187
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,616
Is that him?

188
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:47,451
Sorry, I'll have to ring ya back.

189
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:53,332
Miguel, knock it off!

190
00:13:54,124 --> 00:13:56,710
Stop! I said enough, Miguel!

191
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:04,051
Sorry, folks... Don't mind us.

192
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:06,971
King, you all right?

193
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,473
Yeah...

194
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:16,438
Gone soft, have ya?
Lettin' Miguel wallop ya like that...

195
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,483
Guess I need rehab.

196
00:14:22,069 --> 00:14:23,779
You stable now?

197
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:25,990
I hate to say this, but...

198
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:28,075
Cyberpsychosis?

199
00:14:28,158 --> 00:14:29,994
- Yeah.
- I'm fine.

200
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:32,955
But they shut down all my chrome.

201
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,748
Any reactivation's a death sentence.

202
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:36,584
No shit?

203
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:38,252
Tell me, Meshuga.

204
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:40,921
- What happened then--
- You should've died.

205
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:42,506
Hey...

206
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:45,384
You fuckin' snapped is what happened.

207
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:48,387
If you hadn't lost your shit,
Emily would still be...

208
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:51,140
- Miguel, listen--
- Don't touch me.

209
00:14:52,808 --> 00:14:54,476
Miguel, I...

210
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:57,146
Don't fuckin' touch me, I said.

211
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:01,901
Hey, wait, Miguel! It ain't King's fault...

212
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:03,360
- Lemme go!
- Miguel!

213
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:04,528
Tell me!

214
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:10,117
I can't remember.
What did I do? Did Emily--

215
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,952
You fuckin' killed her!

216
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:13,913
I did?

217
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:19,335
Why... Why's Emily dead,
but your gonk ass gets to live?

218
00:15:19,418 --> 00:15:21,128
Should've died there with her!

219
00:15:21,211 --> 00:15:23,631
What kinda edgerunner are you?

220
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:28,928
Meshuga...

221
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:30,888
You should go.

222
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:32,765
Talk soon, ay?

223
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:40,397
Yooo!

224
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:42,608
Mr. King!

225
00:15:47,571 --> 00:15:51,158
Hey, remember us?

226
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:55,412
'Course ya don't, do ya?

227
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:57,247
The "King's" a big deal!

228
00:15:58,123 --> 00:16:00,000
What's with that look?

229
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:05,005
You chooms ever hear his real name?

230
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:09,385
Weak Kingsley. "Weak" suits him better.

231
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:11,261
Crew-killin' piece of shit!

232
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:14,014
Don't ever show
your face 'round here again!

233
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:30,447
I'm at the building you told me about.
It's sealed up tight.

234
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:32,658
Really sure it's here?

235
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:35,369
'Course. Thereabouts.

236
00:16:35,452 --> 00:16:36,662
"Thereabouts"?

237
00:16:36,745 --> 00:16:38,622
Just poke around.

238
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:42,960
Old fart's no use at all...

239
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:44,188
And who are you?

240
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:50,444
A kid?

241
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:54,114
Uh, I'm sorry. I filmed without asking...

242
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:56,867
Ow...

243
00:17:57,493 --> 00:18:00,662
Sorry, but I thought
it wouldn't be safe to call out.

244
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:04,374
Actually... I'm lookin' for...

245
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:06,960
Maelstrom...

246
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:13,050
You're still mostly 'ganic?

247
00:18:13,133 --> 00:18:14,426
Why?

248
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:19,014
"Why?" I dunno... Not really interested--

249
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,099
Ouch!

250
00:18:20,682 --> 00:18:24,103
How can you be in a body like that?

251
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,605
Whoa! What?

252
00:18:26,688 --> 00:18:27,981
Cross it.

253
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:35,614
Shouldn'ta filmed without askin'.
I'm really sorry...

254
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:37,866
Not what we're talking about right now.

255
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:42,037
You saw me do it.
Now it's my turn to watch you.

256
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,914
No way, I can't!

257
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:44,998
How come?

258
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:47,251
'Cause it's impossible without implants!

259
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:50,712
Yet you think you can
just live without 'em.

260
00:18:51,338 --> 00:18:52,589
So, prove to me you don't.

261
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:01,682
There she is.

262
00:19:01,765 --> 00:19:04,685
Talia! How's the stabilizer runnin'?

263
00:19:04,768 --> 00:19:06,270
Preem. No issues.

264
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,272
Maelstrom...

265
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:09,523
Who's the runt?

266
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:12,401
Yo, he's full 'ganic.

267
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:14,194
You're right. He's not modded at all.

268
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,905
Says he's interested in you guys.

269
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:20,784
That's not... exactly what I meant...

270
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:23,412
Say no more.

271
00:19:23,495 --> 00:19:24,955
Welcome to the club.

272
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:26,748
The club...

273
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:29,418
Stop strugglin'.

274
00:19:29,501 --> 00:19:32,254
Relax, you're gonna look sick.

275
00:19:37,801 --> 00:19:39,303
Later, Talia!

276
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:44,016
Quit your squealin'.

277
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:03,911
Made a wise choice with us, kid.

278
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:06,413
No one wants to be all meat.

279
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:10,125
Been wantin' to give this baby a whirl.

280
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:11,835
Ooh, you got a new toy?

281
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,588
We said no squealin'.

282
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:19,593
Now then...
Want anesthesia or nah?

283
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:22,804
- That a "no"?
- He's so brave!

284
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:25,474
- A kid?
- Whatever you say.

285
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,351
Showtime.

286
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:37,819
Rats... Plan's up in dust.

287
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:40,447
Aaand he's not here.

288
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:42,574
Hey, you all right?

289
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:52,417
Another runner!

290
00:20:57,047 --> 00:21:00,509
Can you get out of here on your own?
Not savin' you twice!

291
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:08,767
Hey.

292
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:14,564
You know him, right? Fella's name
is Helio. Mind tellin' me where he is?

293
00:21:15,565 --> 00:21:17,150
You understand the position you're in?

294
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:19,611
Helio ain't in the gang no more!

295
00:21:20,862 --> 00:21:23,115
I'm asking where the hell he is.

296
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:27,786
Okay, okay, this is where he's holed up!

297
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:31,290
Cool.

298
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:42,592
Ah, my camera!

299
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:46,930
Least I have a backup...

300
00:21:49,224 --> 00:21:50,392
Oh, hey, choom!

301
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:54,730
Phew, I was worried
you might leave through the front--

302
00:21:54,813 --> 00:22:00,610
You brain-dead? Do you realize you coulda
been killed, chopped up, or worse?

303
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:03,488
I appreciate you savin' me.

304
00:22:04,114 --> 00:22:06,616
And I wanna show you my thanks.

305
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:08,660
Your thanks?

306
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:10,620
Well, I happen to live near by.

307
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:14,082
Another round.

308
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:16,543
There is no more.

309
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:20,422
That's the last of it.
Everything we had in the house.

310
00:22:22,049 --> 00:22:23,300
No more thanks?

311
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:26,720
I'll... go buy more.

312
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:46,907
What'm I gonna tell Dad?

313
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:51,661
No point filmin' this...

314
00:22:58,502 --> 00:23:00,921
The hell are those gonks?

315
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:04,674
We gonna sit here and let 'em clown us?

316
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:07,761
- Damn badges think they can step on us!
- Oh shit, my ride!

317
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:08,970
What're you watching?

318
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:14,351
"Burst Panic: The Big Crash."

319
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:17,187
Never heard of it.

320
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:19,606
That's them! We've got 'em!

321
00:23:19,689 --> 00:23:20,941
Kinda figured.

322
00:23:26,071 --> 00:23:28,698
Static-ass streetpunks! Bring it on!

323
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:31,952
It's... set in the Badlands... is it?

324
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:35,205
Yup. It's a nomad flick, after all.

325
00:23:36,039 --> 00:23:37,791
Can it!

326
00:23:38,291 --> 00:23:40,460
Muster some backbone for once!

327
00:23:40,544 --> 00:23:42,045
Who the hell is that?

328
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:47,467
I'm the goddamn sheriff of this land!

329
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:49,719
You scum!

330
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:51,972
Gimme the Lexington.

331
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:56,476
Never thought I'd use a Lexington again...

332
00:23:57,060 --> 00:23:59,646
Takes me back to my rookie days.

333
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,405
Avida...

334
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:14,035
Wish I could've seen you one last time--

335
00:24:16,496 --> 00:24:17,706
Avida?

336
00:24:31,219 --> 00:24:32,762
Avida!

337
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:43,935
Subtitle translation by:
CD PROJEKT RED & Megumi Hunter
